 "notes": {
  "scale": "Plan (x, y) 1:1 to the registered UF floor plans (docs/libwest_layout.md 3); floors 6.0 m apart in the game (real ~4.2 m, estimate): 5.4 m clear for the SM64 camera.",
  "deviations": [
   "Floor-to-floor 6.0 m (real ~4.2 m): camera headroom over 2.3-3.0 m stacks; a floor is not one backflip.",
   "The Plaza Hall: a 25.9 x 12.7 m void over the lobby, 11.4 m tall, behind the real two-storey glass (the real 2nd floor runs up to the glass): the design's 'rotunda' (Act 3 Big Boo) and the night showpiece.",
   "West / east stair halls 7.0 x 10.0 m (real ~3.2 x 7.2 m), NW / NE halls 7.6 x 10.2 m with a roof door onto the north terrace (only the tower boxes are on the plans); 30 deg switchbacks, 3.15-3.45 m lanes.",
   "Escalators: two static 30 deg ramps (switched off after hours), bottom 2.6 m further in for the spawn.",
   "Stacks 1.2 m deep with 3.2 m / 2.86 m aisles (real compact shelving ~0.6 m, no fixed aisles); the 3.6 m rows are built 3.0 m (a jump on top fits under the 5.4 m ceiling), end-cap steps, book-cart bridges.",
   "Doors 2.0-2.6 m wide, 2.6 m tall; glass partitions run floor to ceiling, so every room is sealed except its door gap (no door leaves are modelled in the gaps).",
   "The base roof (z 18) is walkable: west, north and east ROOF TERRACES with 1.1 m parapets, reached by the F4 terrace doors and the NW / NE stair-hall roof doors.",
   "Floor 5 (staff offices, no plan published) is closed except a corridor ring, the staff break room and the electrical room; its stair-hall doors are open gaps in the geometry (the layout's 'locked except Acts 4-5' needs act masks, which static geometry cannot have: the missions add Lua barriers).",
   "Floor 6 reuses floor 4's core; its plaza-face slots become one big view window (Act 1's star).",
   "The main elevators' car A is OUT OF ORDER with its doors open on every floor (a wall-kick shaft, as at Marston); car B, the east elevator and the ADA elevator are closed.",
   "The coffee counter is unbranded and narrower (x 42.0..51.7; the real Starbucks runs to x 58.3).",
   "Entrance: the revolving door and the north doors are locked after hours; nothing outside is walkable. The revolving door's drum is centred on the glass line (the layout's spot is 1 m inside it).",
   "The F3 electrical room's south wall moves 0.9 m north (y 267.6 -> 268.5) and the F5 breaker panel to the electrical room's east wall: the layout put them across the west stair hall's F3 door and in the F5 electrical room's doorway. Free columns within 2.2 m of a stair-hall door and in the north wing's stack aisles are left out.",
   "Rolling ladders, Boos, breakers, the coffee cup and the glowing books are mission devices (Lua), not level geometry; the electrical rooms, the break room and the hide-and-seek spots are in place for them."
  ],
  "fix_round": [
   "Car A's F1 threshold: a 1.7 x 0.2 m floor (+ a metal sill) in the doorway. K.elevator's thresholds are the lintel tops of the storey below, so its lowest floor had none, and the BANK hole in the F1 slab left a 0.2 m strip with no floor (an SM64 invisible wall) that trapped anyone who dropped into the shaft.",
   "Finals-week clutter (visual only): open laptops glowing at about a third of the study seats (each a small cool light), energy-drink cans, and students asleep on the desks of about one table cluster in six.",
   "The far F3 range-top 1-up moved 1.5 m along its range: it shared the spot with the range top's coin."
  ],
